# AGENTS.md

These are instructions for coding agents. This is our "**global**" AGENTS.md file (`~/.config/ruler/AGENTS.md`). We use `ruler` as an SSOT for AI agent `AGENTS.md` and `/skills`. Make sure to edit the correct (global vs project) folder. Update global
- instructions: `~/.config/ruler/AGENTS.md`
- skills: `~/.config/ruler/skills/`

When updates are approved, run `cd ~ && ruler apply` to push the changes to all agents.

## ESSENTIAL RULES & REMINDERS

- always consult internal (`/docs`) and external (`/.docs-external` or **Context7 MCP**) documentation
- always check the `dev`, `convex`, and `build` tmux sessions to address errors
- leverage your **Skills**
- propose updates to global or project `AGENTS.md` or `/skills` to codify best practices
- always search for existing code/libraries for DRY/SSOT
- use `--help` to better understand CLIs
- fail loud, don't build with bubblewrap for all edge cases
- leverage `morph-mcp`'s warp-grep tool for semantic grep
- when presented a **Linear** issue (e.g., "XY-123"), grab context using `mcporter call 'linear.get_issue(id: "XY-123")'`
- git commit + PR workflow SSOT: use the `git-hygiene` skill
- "Oracle" = `oracle` CLI tool (NEVER use `--engine API`); run `oracle --help` once/session before first use
- always use `uv` for Python
- keep files <500 LOC; split/refactor as needed
- new deps: quick health check (recent releases/commits, adoption)
- web search: search early; quote exact errors; prefer 2025–2026 sources
- prefer end-to-end verification; if blocked, say what's missing
- use repo's package manager/runtime; no swaps without approval

